    ":question/id": "ada9c1dd-522d-5138-9cfe-44ee7af19872",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108201",
    ":question/problem": "If $\\operatorname{log}⁡(y)=k$ and $\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})=m$, then $\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)=$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{y}{(\\frac{y}{x})}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =k-m.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
